# Installed by desk as Chromium's flags for every start, from the dash or `chromium URL` from
# another program (Arch: /etc/chromium-flags.conf; Fedora: appended to /etc/chromium/chromium.conf;
# Debian: /etc/chromium.d/desk).
# One per line; a line starting with # is a comment.
# No first-run dialog ("Additional Terms of Service") or tabs.
--no-first-run
# GDM logs in without a password, so there is no unlocked keyring and Chromium would ask for a
# new one's password at its first start.
--password-store=basic
# Pages' web console into its output, which lands in the journal (desk browser console).
--enable-logging=stderr
# The accessibility tree from the start: without it desk a11y saw only the window's frame of a
# Chromium just started.
--force-renderer-accessibility
# An address opened from outside (desk browser open, prepare scripts) replaces the page in the
# current tab, as typing it would, instead of piling up tabs.
--same-tab
# A window as large as the screen, as Firefox's: DevTools' device mode (desk browser viewport)
# shows a phone's page below their toolbar.
--start-maximized
